CON-04: return only the rain on the covered barrel's own footprint

lid_getRunoff() returned subcatch->rainfall * subcatch->lidArea to the
pervious area for every covered rain barrel row. subcatch->lidArea is the
total area of ALL LID units in the subcatchment, so the rain falling on the
other units (which they also take as inflow) was returned a second time,
and once more for each further covered-barrel row. Use the unit's own area
(lidArea = area * number, already computed for the unit).

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b:
    git apply CON-04_swmm530.patch

diff --git a/src/legacy/engine/lid.c b/src/legacy/engine/lid.c
index e2ac45a..395ac7a 100644
--- a/src/legacy/engine/lid.c
+++ b/src/legacy/engine/lid.c
@@ -1702,7 +1702,7 @@ void lid_getRunoff(int j, double tStep)
                 lidProc->storage.covered == TRUE)
             {
                 // Add runoff from closed rain barrel to return (cfs)
-                qReturn += subcatch->rainfall * subcatch->lidArea;
+                qReturn += subcatch->rainfall * lidArea;
 			}
             else
             {
